settings, and adding popups. The guide concludes with a recommendation on whether WoodMart is the right choice for a WooCommerce store.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6c6fec19ce4303d9544eb2185ccb0cb9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T13:29:15.263Z"},{"id":"BWd9nWBPk","title":"Issue #639","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17324734/issue-639","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/issue-639-bwd9nwbpk","summary":"A guide on using lazy loading correctly to improve web performance without causing regressions. Covers when lazy loading helps versus when it backfires, its impact on Core Web Vitals metrics (LCP, CLS, INP), practical implementation patterns, and common real-world pitfalls to avoid.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/24ae8e5d5ff3d32dce8857f2c1f4a8c4?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T11:59:48.180Z"},{"id":"maS7UWSdm","title":"Introducing YouTube Channel Visualizer","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17322890/introducing-youtube-channel-visualizer","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-youtube-channel-visualizer-mas7uwsdm","summary":"YouTube Channel Visualizer is a tool that lets creators visualize their YouTube channel as an interactive diagram, surfacing key metrics like views, tags, and content type. It supports multiple layout modes (Timeline, Tags, Views, Grid, Calendar, Stats), video filtering, localStorage persistence, and PNG export for social media. The video also covers how to build similar visual tools using the JointJS Claude Playground plugin for Claude Code, demonstrating a vibe-coding workflow for creating data visualization apps.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5eb0f0edc666ad96df7705ba62291a95?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-21T12:55:13.047Z"},{"id":"xmdseIg5L","title":"Use CSS Weekly Archives To Find the Best CSS Content & Tools","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17322124/use-css-weekly-archives-to-find-the-best-css-content-tools","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/use-css-weekly-archives-to-find-the-best-css-content-tools-xmdseig5l","summary":"A short video guide showing how to use the CSS Weekly Archives to search for high-quality CSS articles, tutorials, and frontend tools. Covers how search works in the archives, how to browse the full archive history, and why it's a useful resource for finding top CSS content.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2caf6869b28917500be7f4aad0c814f4?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":12,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-20T08:17:43.973Z"},{"id":"d3hAmEI09","title":"Frontend News #22: x86 CPU in CSS, pointer-box-offset Property","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17317255/frontend-news-22-x86-cpu-in-css-pointer-box-offset-property-detecting-at-rule-support","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/frontend-news-22-x86-cpu-in-css-pointer-box-offset-property-d3hamei09","summary":"A curated frontend news roundup covering several CSS topics: detecting at-rule support in CSS, the new pointer-box-offset property for increasing pointer target sizes, different ways to select the HTML element in CSS, a look at the Mole tool, and a creative experiment recreating x86 CPU architecture entirely in CSS.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9a68db599296a5254c90634b1b84e7fd?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-10T23:11:45.964Z"},{"id":"I9dudDEmB","title":"CSS text-indent Keywords?","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17287363/css-text-indent-keywords","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/css-text-indent-keywords--i9duddemb","summary":"A short video guide covering the CSS `text-indent` property's lesser-known keywords: `each-line` and `hanging`. The tutorial walks through how each keyword works, with a demo setup and a look at current browser support.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/25c52b357f84abf0b1e9cd227a82a100?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-01T21:31:40.609Z"},{"id":"GrvyC75oV","title":"Frontend News #20: CSS Grid Lanes, ::search-text Pseudo-Element, HTML Geolocation Element","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17280489/frontend-news-20-css-grid-lanes-search-text-pseudo-element-html-geolocation-element","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/frontend-news-20-css-grid-lanes-search-text-pseudo-element-html-geolocation-element-grvyc75ov","summary":"Frontend News #20 covers several emerging web platform features: CSS Grid Lanes for native masonry layouts, the new `::search-text` pseudo-element for styling in-page search results, a new HTML `<geolocation>` element, a deep dive into how a single emoji character can cause major performance issues, and a CodePen demo of a bubble color picker.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f4e7f1a478fb01d69866e49fff24c9e5?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":18,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-20T23:53:12.894Z"},{"id":"yRN3HZsMy","title":"Issue #636","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17279510/issue-636","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/issue-636-yrn3hzsmy","summary":"CSS Weekly Issue #636 covers the announcement of Interop 2026 by Yulun Wu and Jen Simmons, which continues efforts to improve cross-browser interoperability. The issue also touches on avoiding common CSS mistakes, using Touch ID for SUDO, and building flexible typographic scales.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bf0ed3588d73dd03bcfe9773d43b0f32?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-19T16:40:32.746Z"},{"id":"eTyaiEPsX","title":"How To Use Touch ID for SUDO on macOS","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17275725/how-to-use-touch-id-for-sudo-on-macos","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-use-touch-id-for-sudo-on-macos-etyaiepsx","summary":"macOS 14 (Sonoma) and newer supports Touch ID for sudo commands. Enable it by copying the template file `/etc/pam.d/sudo_local.template` to `/etc/pam.d/sudo_local` and uncommenting the `auth sufficient pam_tid.so` line. This only works locally (not over SSH), and by default doesn't work during screen recording\u2014though that limitation can be bypassed with a defaults write command.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d08ff92be51a9609ac0e91f11d03a6b1?_a=AQAEunF","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-13T10:43:32.171Z"},{"id":"f1ZDIRrLa","title":"Issue #635","url":"https://feedpress.me/link/24028/17275488/issue-635","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/issue-635-f1zdirrla","summary":"CSS Weekly Issue #635 curates recent CSS content including tutorials on the @scope rule for maintainable styling, CSS-only elastic text effects, creating interactive Pantone color decks with native HTML elements, and semantic pie charts without JavaScript. Also features Chrome DevTools tips for targeting elements in the console, SVG icon resources, and creative demos like video text effects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a61378ff4ebabceeac222a2b8c6e6155?_a=AQAEunF","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-13T00:27:12.743Z"}],"similar_handles":["allaboutcoding","robinwieruch","exakat","codimis","tkdodo"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"allaboutcoding","handle":"allaboutcoding","name":"Random Thoughts about Building Software","is_squad":false,"x":-8.1772,"y":7.8251,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":65,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/68eb736adb9a4e519075ffaacd7c5d88","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.416386,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score"